  {
    "episode_id": 95638,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95638.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 2,
    "turn_text": "Welcome to Business Game Changers. I'm Sarah Westall. Today, we're going to dive deeper into the deep state. And I'm going to bring on somebody with a different perspective, somebody who has a ton of background and would have insight from congressional perspective. I'm bringing on Cynthia McKinney, who spent 12 years in Congress. And six terms. And she also was the 2008 Green Party presidential candidate. She's going to come on and share with us her experiences while she was in Congress. There's a video that went viral of her questioning Rumsfeld and others on 9-11. She was one of the few voices in Congress that was willing to take them to task and ask them what was actually going on. And she was one of the most ethical people in Congress because she had an ethics czar in her office and she was squeaky clean so nobody had anything on her. So she was questioning people and digging in and doing her job and she had a lot of enemies. And so she's going to explain that, what happened and her views since. She's also spent time on the ground in Libya and in Syria and understands it from that perspective. And so she's going to share her insights on what's really going on on the ground in Syria and what happened in Libya. and also what's going on in the Middle East in general. We also talk about how and whether it's possible to bring together people of color and people on the right and form a coalition of different people and alternative parties so that we can bring integrity back to our government and whether that's possible. It seems like there's a lot of alignment on major issues from people that think they're on the left and think they're on the right. But really, maybe we're all kind of aligning on certain things. We might not agree with how the government should be run, but we agree on a lot of the big issues. So we're going to talk about that as well. So let's get right into that interview with Cynthia McKinney. Hi, Cynthia. Welcome to the program.",
