    "turn_text": "Well, the mother of all bombs is when I started talking about, well, you know, what really goes on in Washington, DC and who controls DC and, you know, I didn't sign the pledge and, you know, blah, blah, blah and all this sort of stuff. And so, so the 911 thing was, I mean, it lived with me, but it wasn't the, the, the final blow, right? It was when I gathered a conscience, quite frankly, about the votes that Congress cast with respect to Israel and Palestine. And that really was the final blow. And so after I was, I mean, you know, they tried little things to make my life difficult. They actually tried to get me to go along with the program, Cynthia, get a phone call, Cynthia, what are you gonna do this? You know, you can be on the front page of Newsweek in time. You can stay in Congress for as long as you like. You can die there if you want to. That was offered to me. But I had to lie in order to do it. I had to lie in order to stay there. What they particularly wanted for me was. And who was they?",
