    "turn_idx": 58,
    "turn_text": "Well, you see the. The Supreme power in DC is the Israel lobby. In my opinion, people talk about the gun lobby, the insurance lobby. What else? They're very powerful. The bankers, very powerful. But you see, the bankers and the sort of committee specific So, like for example, if you're on the Ways and Means Committee, then you have a certain group of special interests that converge there and they control, you know, basically most of the members of Congress that are there because that's where the money that is raised by those members of Congress come from. So you have a division like, for example, where some committees are known as money committees. and the goal and the dream of most members of Congress is to get on the money committee. Because if you can get on one of those money committees, then the campaign dollars will flow and then you will be able to stay in Congress, you know, you can die there. But there's something, I believe, that dies inside of you. Yes. Okay. And that's why I did all of their tricks. They never worked with me because I wasn't interested. You know, it's what, wine, women and song. I wasn't interested in that. I wasn't interested in money. I just was elected. I was willing to live within my means. to live on my salary and to do the work that came with the job. Now, I understood separation of powers, checks and balances, the role of the legislative branch, the executive",
